[{"id":"VRCE-6-28-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":1,"english":"Those, kings, man and monkey, that monkey the Wind-god's son, Jāmbavān-sovereign of bears—the Rākşasa, Vibhīşaņa, the son of Vālī, Angada, Sumitrā's son, the monkey, Sarabha, Susena along with his friends, Kumuda, Nala, and Panasa, arriving at the dominions of the enemy, assembled together, began to deliberate.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ccbeb5bf4c77d7285a283ce4ee5efe1dedfd9bab5fe3d45c579ff01771580716","compact":"279bbb6ae1bd558478d35bd2079c8636929a44a725d1bcab0ed3597e03fcca65","nasal":"0161c0017ba2ed1e8e52e14a1ad1e6986a8b3ad2a787f2bc1624b7435824a52b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":2,"english":"Those, kings, man and monkey, that monkey the Wind-god's son, Jāmbavān-sovereign of bears—the Rākşasa, Vibhīşaņa, the son of Vālī, Angada, Sumitrā's son, the monkey, Sarabha, Susena along with his friends, Kumuda, Nala, and Panasa, arriving at the dominions of the enemy, assembled together, began to deliberate.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7790ad456229e5e4e3271d3017ad7a6e9b7c525ef5e9b959bfad62ad6c72cbb5","compact":"837e401f5b0c1cdc7722784dc6a82faf0d19c819f6e753d7187f11aec1e90436","nasal":"577d697c2d20e2a89ace30e1a7b0bd4cb6dd06e8bb5e49812d4c7004f94a7f4e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":3,"english":"Those, kings, man and monkey, that monkey the Wind-god's son, Jāmbavān-sovereign of bears—the Rākşasa, Vibhīşaņa, the son of Vālī, Angada, Sumitrā's son, the monkey, Sarabha, Susena along with his friends, Kumuda, Nala, and Panasa, arriving at the dominions of the enemy, assembled together, began to deliberate.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a7c04234f2bdeeeca85aada532955cfb4203cebf63a6922da56bed70ffffb34","compact":"4232c41d29d1707e24c361e1f7165c9b4fe741f06385735f2f65ac104a36a6de","nasal":"4232c41d29d1707e24c361e1f7165c9b4fe741f06385735f2f65ac104a36a6de"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":4,"english":"Yonder is that Lankā ruled by Rāvana, invincible even to the celestials, serpents and Gandharvas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.745,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43fe9228cae597356a2c82da521ec201f816393dfa5ddf56389911265ec7d2d2","compact":"75245e40b80be330ee20ef7898b0d9bbf870f4a4b7a0dad1963c6b1e9634fe88","nasal":"58440d73a56a24af107286e368aa584b28d3b3e281efc31648b540df0b0850ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":5,"english":"Let us, keeping before us success in the enterprise, consult together for the purpose of arriving at a decision.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adc4c4d9c92e84912c6e532ddcb140cae4b240d9cdb2a73b41d7c7d6cdaa2669","compact":"2ce41dc02ee379d3d88da1c805d993cb9a260fd309d624bca2f949795ee43920","nasal":"271d6d7f48d14cec2449f42b642e4facfc9c0b6fd3482aa53a919a7f41d0f145"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":6,"english":"We are here daily nearing Răvaņa, lord of Raksasas. As they were speaking thus, Ravana's younger brother, Vibhīşaņa, said in a pregnant speech free from provinicialism.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9958edfb5f453166ef40f7c459a1da136bd06fcac7c83ebd6b633777a2e6979","compact":"f0eee64f64b9b358f2fe6373a829b82122f83e55b917d28a7529daa404081d65","nasal":"f0eee64f64b9b358f2fe6373a829b82122f83e55b917d28a7529daa404081d65"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":7,"english":"Anala, Panasa, Sampāti and Pramāti— all courtiers of mine-having gone up to Lanka, have come back here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"075f4e60b42b4d68afa88ac81d36b5bfcc30ca46cc955f6bd1ac6838d1180c85","compact":"6e74dd46a30da0bf08c50431a33c62f29e956a0d7a109aeb03ae02943783bd55","nasal":"6c447f044ca5c4576576f8f89bf8507ca13dc54e19dbf4d9684c45c24a5256f7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":8,"english":"Wearing the forms of birds, they entered into the hostile forces; and, having seen the measures that had been adopted (by them, have come (back).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0073e1f66d858ed8b032656dbe822a5f3499ee24811d6eb85b5c3289c8fa045c","compact":"2d8d33f42ee4b28d4cb7ef9e09b79d4b98505c9ddd903398a47a3fb82bbd7ed4","nasal":"2d8d33f42ee4b28d4cb7ef9e09b79d4b98505c9ddd903398a47a3fb82bbd7ed4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":9,"english":"O Rāma, hearken to me as I tell you truly anent the provisions which they have related, made by the wicked-minded Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.729,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6d7f224804da4830b4de0e56d0a85b96063fee5c782694f76476182ce227e17f","compact":"ba05bdf6df3b680688fd603dea7807acb0bc1688b0e205f6fd5485e2155da91c","nasal":"ba05bdf6df3b680688fd603dea7807acb0bc1688b0e205f6fd5485e2155da91c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":10,"english":"In the Eastern gate stay Prahasta along with his forces; in the Southern, the exceedingly powerful Mahāpārsva and Mahodara, and in the Western. Ravana's son, Indrajit, supported by innumerable Räkşasas, equipped with pattiśas, swords and bows, and bearing darts and maces in their hands, surrounded by heroes carrying various weapons.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3e1f9b80491c0581a522f063f5cae805cdd7257ed7878f92acacded75d58e95","compact":"b3feb229a2cebd688ab98ae5b04a805b8d45f4ec297eb26516aa6c35d7989b7c","nasal":"b3feb229a2cebd688ab98ae5b04a805b8d45f4ec297eb26516aa6c35d7989b7c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":11,"english":"In the Eastern gate stay Prahasta along with his forces; in the Southern, the exceedingly powerful Mahāpārsva and Mahodara, and in the Western. Ravana's son, Indrajit, supported by innumerable Räkşasas, equipped with pattiśas, swords and bows, and bearing darts and maces in their hands, surrounded by heroes carrying various weapons.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.786,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd5b5cd15db08a415b6461d0422e8ed70b5b63d69c0a3f061bfee4677f830919","compact":"17246b60af056505b19aaab2d443cadcf7b5297a30de0cc4e649d9987d48996a","nasal":"4b6587d391156aede570e8b9bdcb4baebffc014716b3197adca26e58cbb69dea"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":12,"english":"In the Eastern gate stay Prahasta along with his forces; in the Southern, the exceedingly powerful Mahāpārsva and Mahodara, and in the Western. Ravana's son, Indrajit, supported by innumerable Räkşasas, equipped with pattiśas, swords and bows, and bearing darts and maces in their hands, surrounded by heroes carrying various weapons. And, backed by many thousands of Räkşasas wielding weapons, and accompanied by Rākşasas conversant with counsel, Rāvana himself, his heart agitated to the height, gaurd the Northern gate of the city.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.406,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-8","DUTT-6-37-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eea2950666e5e623667829e63c021cdd68e0fe6551d134a634cbf89d0c7096c7","compact":"daf6e6970a829fd92198d3b67310533ddef579a643005dd80ccb326953fc6c93","nasal":"daf6e6970a829fd92198d3b67310533ddef579a643005dd80ccb326953fc6c93"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":13,"english":"And, backed by many thousands of Räkşasas wielding weapons, and accompanied by Rākşasas conversant with counsel, Rāvana himself, his heart agitated to the height, gaurd the Northern gate of the city.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1680fcf927454d666ed602b222db6ab734d1571480f80eac3db9c6719639830b","compact":"e10d76264dba37cde1bf2ec5149f115085d85b555d88b32572ad437e8e8b95d8","nasal":"e10d76264dba37cde1bf2ec5149f115085d85b555d88b32572ad437e8e8b95d8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":14,"english":"Virüpākṣa with a powerful force accoutred in javelins, clubs and bows, protects the garrison in the centre.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"511515245ee098aca40df64821f4eee4c43eb77c8a33c53d268fb28fa3700045","compact":"f0f64c995a272076749fa8d20e20aac2b462596370cb81937746f9c6f5d46fb1","nasal":"f0f64c995a272076749fa8d20e20aac2b462596370cb81937746f9c6f5d46fb1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":15,"english":"Having seen these hosts thus disposed in Lankä, my counsellors have speedily come back here.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21253664ed02b39c7d69aba238ce7053cb30a7306304ad92235ff51ad60ac2e7","compact":"46052ec76aa747549dd499b9437bfc3c270bb0e7756c366cff36ff9e64d7c61b","nasal":"b39b8369b43e497bbf4d6636db17f640cbaebb262e376250e9ee79e39f08465b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":16,"english":"There are ten thousand elephants, an Ayuta cars, two of horses, and abouta koti of Raksasas, powerful and strong, and equipped with arms in conflict.* *These are, remarks the commentator, the leader.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f334fc243bfbc4166c8c34d29f5acdb9d4a3b65c78c00f5d5cbb7733400e1f17","compact":"b95e9ee6cf0d69238d4963633616cd261c5f6c6de0a95448eb09e17322706154","nasal":"b95e9ee6cf0d69238d4963633616cd261c5f6c6de0a95448eb09e17322706154"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":17,"english":"These night-rangers are ever the favourites of the Raksasa ruler. And, O kine, a koti of forces accompany each of these Rākşasas in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac60c7ac3db399f40e0aee24608149fdb4d2dce151a8bb043a2523439972a6eb","compact":"2d88d21a0a24e706aa21ebc7850f91ac4582c5a4f9d85edae5477c3765383667","nasal":"4b217f69167ced2adaa78d5471f5a08b6a88f55954d0af8099fa11e2e023d384"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":18,"english":"These night-rangers are ever the favourites of the Raksasa ruler. And, O kine, a koti of forces accompany each of these Rākşasas in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bdfc737a5618b915e1eeb2a75fc8cdee31de4e81bb33eba78599d8fdd5d47c0c","compact":"7fb7b625f9f352ece5d3529f5fb2d0eba610defd4cb159e7e55244a16e46ebd8","nasal":"7fb7b625f9f352ece5d3529f5fb2d0eba610defd4cb159e7e55244a16e46ebd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":19,"english":"Having conveyed this information concerning Lankā, which had been communicated by his counsellors, the mighty-armed Vibhīşaņa showed (to Rama) those Raksasas themselves. In company with his counsellors, Ravana's graceful younger brother, ever striving for the welfare of Rama, by way of answer communicated everything that was going forward in Lankā to Räma, having eyes resembling lotus leaves.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.435,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-14","DUTT-6-37-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c6267af53ba9829c456282677cb2c106cd4d2328870cb59110f64c9ae97eec9d","compact":"29127ded39c032710bf062e7ee0faed967c85a13a9b021609ba2a1413b37bde9","nasal":"b921457a9182498151811cac61d5462b74c1438da49ab796957521e5ab524399"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":20,"english":"O Răma, when Rāvana battled with Kuvera, sixty lacs of Raksasas marched forth (to meet him). In prowess, energy, vigour, exceeding fortitude, and hauteur, they resembled the wicked-minded Ravana himself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1cc7fc814cd6b91ef6e8fc5ee5213174b155d7558a1c14979b0c13df2ca88f11","compact":"132e98fc2bb2ed0d7df1be494aa4641f12964b41209d1fb89ecc8119a3902638","nasal":"78fa56b7a37e931801654207004f1a7cb98ae029959d6374e5e8fba481d0152a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":21,"english":"O Răma, when Rāvana battled with Kuvera, sixty lacs of Raksasas marched forth (to meet him). In prowess, energy, vigour, exceeding fortitude, and hauteur, they resembled the wicked-minded Ravana himself.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b17ef417b94ef7c418922b87424c6ca2df60821e1d49fffa751df5f4b477f19d","compact":"9cb5ecffed6b8c57287e32d35b8c7f2b6367de735f95f39e828c651440953abc","nasal":"9cb5ecffed6b8c57287e32d35b8c7f2b6367de735f95f39e828c651440953abc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":22,"english":"In this matter, you ought not to grow wroth, I only arouse your wrath, and do not endeavour to frighten you. You can subdue even the celestials by your prowess. *i.e. You ought not to be angry with me; for I do not frighten you, but rouse your wrath against Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90f710a1ca79b22ca8b1a490e21d1f356725918c92277e5acaf4b3a37e73bcbe","compact":"1c3796a9d230b677626c9775d730531bbe4cd0a456205e04320bed7b4894d844","nasal":"1c3796a9d230b677626c9775d730531bbe4cd0a456205e04320bed7b4894d844"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-28-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":28,"verse":23,"english":"Therefore you, environed by a mighty army, having arrayed the monkey-forces in order of battle, shall thrash Ravana (in battle)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-37-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6028023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d0f18bb9e0401b8a041322046f01835e615be08220400fcc2cf600d886a95c5","comp